      <text xml:space="preserve">:''''' Tlaxcala''' is the name of both a state in Mexico and that state's capital city. This article is about the city. For the state, see: [[Tlaxcala]].''

The city of '''Tlaxcala''' is the capital and chief center of population of the [[Mexico|Mexican]] state of the same name. The city is located at {{coor dm|19|31|N|98|24|W|}}
&lt;!--- 19.31°&amp;nbsp;N, 98.24°&amp;nbsp;W, ---&gt;
and it reported a population of 73,184 in the 2000 census. 

The city, though originally settled by [[Native American (Americas)|native peoples]], was officially &quot;founded&quot; in [[1520]] by [[Hernán Cortés]] &amp;ndash; with whom they had an alliance against their former [[Aztec]] oppressors.

