'''''Chill Out''''' is an album by [[reggae]] band [[Black Uhuru]], released in [[1982]] (see [[1982 in music]]).  The album was recorded at [[Channel One (studio)|Channel One]] in [[Jamaica]] and [[record producer|produced]] by [[Sly &amp; Robbie]].  Featuring [[The Revolutionaries]], an influential session group, ''Chill Out'', together with its dub companion ''The Dub Factor'', is widely considered a classic of reggae music.

''Chill Out'' peaked at #156 on [[Billboard Music Charts|Billboard]]'s (North America) Pop Albums chart.

==Track listing==
