'''''Black Star''''' is the self-titled debut for [[Black Star (hip hop group)|Black Star]] - the pairing of [[rap music| rappers]] [[Talib Kweli]] and [[Mos Def]]. It is sometimes listed as ''Mos Def and Talib Kweli are Black Star''. The album was released on 26 August, 1998.
The title is a reference to a [[shipping]] line founded by [[Pan-Africanism|Pan-Africanist]] [[Marcus Garvey]]. ''Black Star'' deals with modern day issues, thinkings, and life in [[Brooklyn]], [[New York City]] as the two artists know it. They are adept at rapping in any style, whether focusing on a single theme as found on &quot;Astronomy (8th Light)&quot;, which revolves around the color of black, to party rapping as found on &quot;B Boys Will B Boys&quot;.


