  <page>
    <title>Type</title>
    <id>199800</id>
    <revision>
      <id>38303674</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-05T12:24:36Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Mgekelly</username>
        <id>74199</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Type''' has historically had the following uses:

*In [[biology]], a '''[[biological type|type]]''' is the specimen or specimens upon which an original [[species]] description is based.

*In [[computer science]], a '''[[datatype]]''' (sometimes referred to as a 'type') is a collection of values used for computation.

*In [[printing]], '''type''' refers to the metal forms of the letters used in [[typesetting]].

*In [[sociology]], the terms '''[[normal type]]''' and '''[[ideal type]]''' are used.

*In [[My type (dating)|dating]], the term [[my type (dating) | my type]] refers to a potential partner that suits ''my'' taste.

*In [[philosophical logic]], [[Bertrand Russell]] used his '''[[Type theory|Theory of Types]]''' to further discuss the mapping of [[mathematics]] to [[logic]].

*In [[metaphysics]], [[Type (metaphysics)]].

*In [[set theory]] and [[musical set theory]], see [[equivalence class]].

*In [[model theory]], a branch of mathematics, see [[type (model theory)]].

*In [[intuitionistic type theory]], a type can be a [[proposition]] or a [[set]].

*In [[metaphysics]] or [[ontology]], '''type''' may have yet another meaning, see, [[Type (metaphysics)]].

*In [[bible|biblical]] [[theology]], a [[type (theology)|type]] is something in the Bible which  foreshadows things to come.

*In [[music]], [[Type (band)|Type]] is a band name used by [[Portugal|Portuguese]] [[Disc Jockey|DJ]] and musician Cyz (Cynthia Zamorano). 

See also: [[Typology]], the study of types.

{{disambig}}

[[da:Type]]
[[de:Typ]]
[[ja:型]]
[[ru:Тип]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
