  <page>
    <title>British Fifty Pence coin</title>
    <id>199913</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41311430</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-26T13:33:14Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>80.195.225.73</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Large */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The [[United Kingdom|British]] decimal '''fifty [[penny|pence]] (50p)''' [[coin]] was issued on [[October 14]], [[1969]] in the run-up to decimalisation to replace the [[Bank of England#10/-|ten shilling note]].

The coin is minted from an [[alloy]] of 75% [[copper]] and 25% [[nickel]]. Between 1969 and 1997 the coin weighed 13.50 grams and had a diameter of 30.0 millimetres. In 1997 the coin was reduced in size to weigh 8.00 grams and have a diameter of 27.3 millimetres. Note that the coin is not circular but an [[equilateral curve|equilaterally curved]] [[heptagon]] (seven-sided) to aid identification -- the sides are not straight but are curved so that the centre of curvature is the opposite apex of the coin, allowing the coin to roll freely and have its diameter measured correctly in [[slot machine]]s (see also: [[Curve of constant width|curve of constant width]]). This shape was also later used for the [[British coin Twenty Pence|Twenty Pence piece]].

This denomination has frequently been used for commemorative purposes, and consequently there are more design variations in this coin than in any other current British denomination.

The normal reverse of the coin, designed by [[Christopher Ironside]], depicts the seated [[Britannia]] with a [[lion]], with the numeral &quot;50&quot; beneath, and either &lt;small&gt;NEW PENCE&lt;/small&gt; (1969-1981) or &lt;small&gt;FIFTY PENCE&lt;/small&gt; (since 1982) above Britannia.

During the history of the coin, three different obverses have been used so far - between 1969 and 1984 the head of Queen [[Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom|Elizabeth II]] by [[Arnold Machin]] was used, between 1985 and 1997 the head by [[Raphael Maklouf]] was used, and since 1998 one by [[Ian Rank-Broadley]] has been used.

==Variations==
Up to 2005 there have been fourteen varieties of 50p coin, six large and eight small, as follows:

===Large===
[[Image:50POLDBRITANNIA.jpg|right|90px|]]
:1969-1972, 1974-1981
::Obverse: Machin head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] date&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the right of the head.
::Reverse: Britannia and lion, &lt;small&gt;50&lt;/small&gt; below &lt;small&gt;NEW PENCE&lt;/small&gt; above.
::Dates 1971-1972 and 1974-1975 were issued in collector's sets only.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50PRINGOFHANDS.jpg|right|90px|50p coin commemorating Britains accession to the EEC]]
:1973: Commemorates the UK's accession to the [[European Economic Community]].
::Obverse: Machin head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]]&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the right of the head, no date. 
::Reverse: Nine clasped hands, &lt;small&gt;1973 50 PENCE&lt;/small&gt; in the centre.
::The design originally had the word &lt;small&gt;EUROPE&lt;/small&gt; in the middle, but this was vetoed by the [[Foreign and Commonwealth Office]].
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50PREVISEDBRITANNIA.jpg|right|90px|]]
:1982-1984
::Obverse: Machin head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] date&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the right of the head.
::Reverse: Britannia and lion, &lt;small&gt;50&lt;/small&gt; below &lt;small&gt;FIFTY PENCE&lt;/small&gt; above.
::Date 1984 only available in collector's sets.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50PREVISEDBRITANNIA.jpg|right|90px|]]
:1985-1993, 1995-1997
::Obverse: Maklouf head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] date&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head.
::Reverse: Britannia and lion, &lt;small&gt;50&lt;/small&gt; below &lt;small&gt;FIFTY PENCE&lt;/small&gt; above.
::All dates except 1985 available in collector's sets only.  Demand for the 50p coin decreased with the issue of [[British One Pound coin|One Pound]] coins in 1983.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50PCOUNCILOFMINISTERS.jpg|right|90px|1992/3 British Presidency of EC 50p coin]]
:1992-3: Commemorates the completion of the EC single market and the British presidency of the EC.
::Obverse: Maklouf head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]]&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head.
::Reverse: Conference table with seats and stars, &lt;small&gt;50 PENCE&lt;/small&gt; below, &lt;small&gt;1992 1993&lt;/small&gt; above.
::Very few issued into circulation.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50p-dday1994-reverse.jpg|right|90px|1994 D-Day Commemorative 50p coin]]
:1994: 50th anniversary of [[D-Day]].
::Obverse: Maklouf head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 1994&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head.
::Reverse: An invasion force of ships and planes, &lt;small&gt;50 PENCE&lt;/small&gt; to the right.
&lt;br&gt;

===Small===
[[Image:50PREVISEDBRITANNIA.jpg|right|90px|]]
:1997
::Obverse: Maklouf head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 1997&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head.
::Reverse: Britannia and lion, &lt;small&gt;50&lt;/small&gt; below &lt;small&gt;FIFTY PENCE&lt;/small&gt; above.
::Issued only in 1997, but in very large numbers as it had to replace all the earlier types of 50p coin, which were withdrawn from circulation within 6 months.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50PREVISEDBRITANNIA.jpg|right|90px|]]
:1998-date
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] date&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Britannia and lion, &lt;small&gt;50&lt;/small&gt; below &lt;small&gt;FIFTY PENCE&lt;/small&gt; above.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:Uk50p1998EU.jpg|right|90px|1998 EU Commemorative 50p coin]]
:1998: 25th anniversary of Britain joining the [[EU]].
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] date&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Looks like a firework display of 12 stars with &lt;small&gt;1973 EU 1998&lt;/small&gt; underneath and &lt;small&gt;50 PENCE&lt;/small&gt; below.
::5 million minted, but not often found in circulation.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:uk50p1998.jpg|right|90px|1998 NHS Commemorative 50p coin]]
:1998: 50th anniversary of the [[British National Health Service|National Health Service]].
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] date&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Caring hands holding sun's rays &lt;small&gt;FIFTIETH ANNIVERSARY&lt;/small&gt; above and &lt;small&gt;50 PENCE&lt;/small&gt; below, &lt;small&gt;NHS&lt;/small&gt; repeated 5 times around the border. 
::5 million minted, but not often found in circulation.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:uk50p2000.jpg|right|90px|1998 Public Libraries Commemorative 50p coin]]
:2000: 150th anniversary of the Public Libraries Act of 1850.
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 2000&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Open book above pillared building inscribed &lt;small&gt;PUBLIC LIBRARIES 1850 2000&lt;/small&gt; above and &lt;small&gt;50 PENCE&lt;/small&gt; to the right.
::5 million minted, but not often found in circulation.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:uk50p2003vote.jpg|right|90px|2003 Suffragettes Commemorative 50p coin]]
:2003: Centenary of the Women's Social and Political Union (the [[Suffragette]]s).
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 2003&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Suffragette chained to railing holding a banner inscribed WSPU in her left hand, &lt;small&gt;50 PENCE&lt;/small&gt; to the left and a billboard inscribed &lt;small&gt;GIVE WOMEN THE VOTE&lt;/small&gt; to the right, with &lt;small&gt;1903&lt;/small&gt; below and &lt;small&gt;2003&lt;/small&gt; to the right.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50p-4minutemile.jpg|right|90px|2004 four-minute-mile Commemorative 50p coin]]
:2004: 50th Anniversary of first sub-four-minute mile, [[Roger Bannister]], [[6 May]] [[1954]].
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 2004&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Lower body of a runner, superimposed on a stopwatch showing 3 minutes 59 seconds. Large &lt;small&gt;50&lt;/small&gt; and &lt;small&gt;PENCE&lt;/small&gt; at bottom, between runner's legs.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[[Image:50PENCE05.jpg|right|90px|2005 Johnson's Dictionary Commemorative 50p coin]]
:2005: 250th Anniversary of the publication of [[Samuel Johnson]]'s 'Dictionary of the English Language'.
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 2005&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Number 50 at top, with the dictionary definition of 'fifty' and 'pence'
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
:2006: 150th Anniversary of the [[Victoria Cross]].
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 2005&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Pictures of both sides of the Victoria Cross, the reverse engraved 29 JAN 1856. VC FIFTY PENCE below. Designed by Claire Aldridge.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
:2006: 150th Anniversary of the [[Victoria Cross]].
::Obverse: Rank-Broadley head, inscription &lt;small&gt;ELIZABETH II [[British coinage#D.G.REG.F.D.|D G REG F D]] 2005&lt;/small&gt;, starting to the bottom left of the head, &lt;small&gt;IRB&lt;/small&gt; under the bust.
::Reverse: Soldier carrying wounded comrade, FIFTY PENCE below. Designed by Clive Duncan.

==External links==
