      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Fulton Mackay''' ([[August 12]], [[1922]] - [[June 6]], [[1987]]) was a [[Scotland|Scottish]] [[actor]].

Mackay was born in [[Paisley, Scotland]].  He appeared in several films and television programmes, but is best remembered for his role as the warder, [[Mr Mackay]], in the [[British sitcom]], ''[[Porridge (TV)]]''.  He also played a leading role in the hit film, ''[[Local Hero]]'' ([[1983]]) and was the original lighthouse-keeper in the British version of the children's series, ''[[Fraggle Rock]]''.

He also played misguided scientist Doctor Quinn in the ''[[Doctor Who]]'' story ''[[Doctor Who and the Silurians]]'' in [[1970]].

