      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;!-- Unsourced image removed: [[Image:Lowry.jpg|thumb|]] --&gt;
'''Lois Lowry''' ([[March 20]], [[1937]]) is an [[author]] from the [[United States]]. She was born in Hawaii to an [[U.S. Army|army]] family, who named her &quot;Sena&quot;  for her [[Norway|Norwegian]] grandmother; hearing of this, her grandmother [[telegram|telegraphed]] and instructed her parents that the child should have an American name.[http://www.loislowry.com/pdf/Richmond_Speech.pdf]  (Lois and Ann were the names of her father's sisters.)  Her most famous book, ''[[The Giver]]'', is popular yet controversial, and it has been banned in some schools.  

