  <page>
    <title>Nicolas Eugène Géruzez</title>
    <id>200004</id>
    <revision>
      <id>35979572</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-20T17:54:49Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>TimBentley</username>
        <id>531594</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>better link</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Nicolas Eugène Géruzez''' ([[January 6]], [[1799]] - [[May 29]], [[1865]]), was a [[France|French]] [[critic]].

He was born at [[Reims]].  He was assistant professor at the [[University of Paris|Sorbonne]], and in [[1852]] he became secretary to the faculty of literature. His works include a ''Histoire de l'éloquence politique et religieuse en France aux XIV', XV' et XVI' siècles'' (1837-1838); an ''Histoire de la littérature française depuis les origines jusqu&amp;#8217;a la Revolution'' (1852), which he supplemented in 1859 by a volume bringing down the history to the close of the revolutionary period; and some miscellaneous works.

Géruzez died in [[Paris]]. A posthumous volume of ''Mélanges et pensées'' appeared in 1877.

==References==
*{{1911}}

[[Category:1799 births|Géruzez, Nicolas Eugène]]
[[Category:1865 deaths|Géruzez, Nicolas Eugène]]
[[Category:French writers|Géruzez, Nicolas Eugène]]

[[fr:Nicolas Eugène Géruzez]]</text>
    </revision>
