'''''E 1999 Eternal''''' is a [[gangsta rap]] album by [[hip hop music|hip hop]] group  [[Bone Thugs N Harmony]], released on [[July 25]], [[1995]] (see [[1995 in music]]).  following up on the surprise success of their breakthrough single, &quot;Thuggish Ruggish Bone&quot;, ''E 1999 Eternal'' became a popular album that received substantial critical acclaim for Bone Thugs N Harmony's unique melodic style of [[rapping]].

''E 1999 Eternal'' peaked on [[Billboard Music Charts|Billboard]]'s (North America) Top R&amp;B/Hip Hop Albums and the Billboard 200 charts.

==Track listing==
#&quot;Da Introduction&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek/T. Hester)
#&quot;East 1999&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek/Tony-C)
#&quot;Eternal&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek/Tony-C)
#&quot;Crept and We Came&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek)
#&quot;Down '71 (The Getaway)&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek/Tony-C)
#&quot;Mr.
#&quot;Mr. Ouija 2&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek)
#&quot;[[Mo' Murda]]&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek/Tony-C)
#&quot;Shotz to Tha Double Glock&quot; (Bone/D.J. U-Neek/Poetic Hustlas/Graveyard Shift/Kenny McCloud)

