      <comment>Re-categorisation per [[Wikipedia:Categories for deletion]].</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Jesse Lynch Williams''' ([[1871]]-[[1929]]) was an [[United States|American]] [[Pulitzer Prize for Drama|Pulizer-Prize]]-winning [[author]] and [[dramatist]]. 

Williams began his literary career in college, writing ''Princeton Stories.'' Upon graduation he continued to write [[novel]]s and [[play]]s, including ''Why Marry?'' for which he was awarded the first [[Pulitzer Prize for Drama]] in [[1918]].

Works by Jesse Lynch Williams:

'''Novels and Short Stories:'''
*''Princeton Stories''
*''The Adventures of a Freshman''
*''The Girl and the Game''

'''Plays:'''
*''Lovely Lady''
*''Why Marry?''
*''The Stolen Story''
{{US-writer-stub}}

[[Category:1871 births|Williams, Jesse Lynch]]
[[Category:1929 deaths|Williams, Jesse Lynch]]
[[Category:Pulitzer Prize winners|Williams, Jesse Lynch]]
[[Category:American dramatists and playwrights|Williams, Jesse Lynch]]</text>
    </revision>
